  "id": "principle-of-similarity",
  "term": "principle of similarity",
  "definition": "In this historical source, the principle of similarity means giving the same punishment for the same offence on the assumption that offenders are alike. The passage argues that, because offenders differ greatly in their bodily, mental, and social conditions, this principle is unfair and does not work well in practice.",
